  "rationale": "The representative failure is a noun following an opening determiner: apples and needles receive almost no probability after “The,” despite the batch repeatedly using noun phrases such as “The small needles,” “The small pears,” and “One morning.” Existing noun rules favor contexts involving verbs or other suffixes, while some other nouns already have strong determiner-context rules. Add a compact suffix pattern for nouns that occur in these noun phrases; the optional adjective run allows both bare and modified nouns. This is a lexicalized, limited repair rather than a claim that every noun fits every determiner context. Other continuations, including adjectives and different nouns, should remain possible. The prior structural candidate was rejected in favor of a weight-only update, with replay regression among the concerns, so this patch avoids new heads and limits changes to a few supported noun roots. Possible counterexamples include contexts where a determiner is followed by a noun outside this set, or where these nouns are not appropriate; the replay gate must assess the tradeoff.",
